"""F7 Boolean factor lexicon per domain pack (Claude-written seeds; spec 2.2 factor names, U02 kinds, U03 banned kinds).

Why it exists: the packs' Boolean fields are participial status phrases ("deposit received", "hours verified") that
cannot fill the F7 criterion forms "<X> occurred" / "<X> is in place" (3.1 "Criterion negation"). packs-1 handed F7
the job of building concept sets (manifest handoff "F7 U01 concept sets"). Each pack below gets 10 noun-phrase
factors written for its domain: kind E (event: "<X> occurred") or S (state: "<X> is in place"), polarity + (adverse) or
- (favourable), term | alias. A leading "~" marks a mass noun used without an article.
Every entry is linted by f7packs.lint_name (negation, banned stems, partial / multiplicity words, operator words,
digits) and is decontaminated with the rows (sealed_check on every output row; 7.2 counts-only runs by the orchestrator).
"""

